From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo: keep LVS7 on

PM8921 LVS7 also supplies the Krait CPU and L2 HFPLLs: the downstream
board file maps it to krait0..3_hfpll and l2_hfpll voters. Here only the
DSI host, the DSI PHY and the panel use it, so it is switched off whenever
all three are powered down, stopping every core that runs above the
384 MHz auxiliary rate. Mark it always-on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
@@ -386,9 +386,15 @@
 		/*
 		 * mipi_dsi.1-dsi1_vddio
 		 * pil_riva-pll_vdd
+		 *
+		 * Also the 1.8 V supply of the Krait CPU and L2 HFPLLs: the
+		 * downstream kernel keeps it on with "krait*_hfpll" and
+		 * "l2_hfpll" votes. Nothing votes for those here, so do not let
+		 * the display turn it off while the CPUs run from the HFPLLs.
 		 */
 		pm8921_lvs7: lvs7 {
 			bias-pull-down;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 	};
 };
